Release notes for fastent. See ChangeLog for source-level changes.

v1.3 (2026-05-20)
- Move LZ77F and Bandt-Pompe permutation entropy to `-e`.
- Add the NIST 32x32 binary matrix-rank test to `-eee`.
- Add a fixed-window Maurer universal test to `-eee`.
- Add a 512-bit Berlekamp-Massey linear-complexity test to `-eee`.
- Report and plot each new estimator in plain, CSV, JSON, recursive, and
  annotated output.

v1.2 (2026-05-16)
- Make `-e` repeatable. `-ee` adds order-1 entropy, mutual information, runs,
  longest run, and bit cusum.
- Add min-entropy, collision entropy, index of coincidence, poker, variance,
  redundancy, symbol counts, and bit-position bias to `-e`.
- Add the `--annotate` PASS, WEAK, and FAIL report.
- Add FIPS 140-2 monobit, poker, runs, and long-run tests.
- Add JSON, recursive CSV/JSON, sorting, terminal histograms, explicit I/O
  selection, and short option aliases.
- Make floating-point results stable across supported hosts.

v1.1 (2026-05-12)
- Add NEON, SVE2, AVX-512 BITALG, and WebAssembly SIMD128 kernels.
- Add io_uring on Linux and IOCP on Windows.
- Add recursive mode and terminal histograms.
- Add WebAssembly, DJGPP/MS-DOS, Windows 95, and further Linux release targets.
- Add UTF-8 paths on modern Windows and native worker threads.

v1.0 (2026-05-08)
- First release.
- Report Shannon entropy, chi-square, arithmetic mean, Monte Carlo pi, and
  serial correlation for byte or bit streams.
- Dispatch scalar, SSSE3, SSE4.1, AVX2, and AVX-512 kernels at run time.
- Support mapped or streamed input and deterministic worker-thread reduction.
